      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is about twice the usual maximum:\n- **Immediate-release:** the maximum is 2,550 mg/day, usually given as 850 mg three times daily.\n- **Extended-release:** the maximum is 2,000\u20132,500 mg/day.\n\nA dose this high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and severe GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nWhich of these did you mean?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals:** 2,550 mg/day, the maximum.\n- **1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals:** 2,000 mg/day.\n- **500 mg or 850 mg PO twice or three times daily:** a typical starting or titration dose.\n- **Another dose:** if 1,700 mg was intended, for example as a daily total, tell me and I'll enter it that way.\n\nIf you want exactly 1,700 mg three times daily, please confirm that it's intentional. I can enter it with a note, but I'd suggest checking with pharmacy first."
      }
